+// The scalar original paid two bounds tests, an index computation and a kernel-type switch per tap per
+// output; for WakeHuBERT's dilated K=5 depthwise convs that held them at roughly a tenth of the 1x1
+// convs' GFLOP/s. Per output the taps are still accumulated in (ky, kx) order starting from 0, as the
+// scalar loop does, so the only numerical change is FMA contraction inside the SIMD sweep.
 static void ggml_compute_forward_conv_2d_dw_whcn(
